module

public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.Current.CoordinateAction
public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.Current.Field

/-!
# The vacuum module of a residue central extension

Let `ĝ = L((t)) ⊕ R K` be the residue central extension of an invariant symmetric form `Φ`, and let
`U = U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` be its enveloping algebra at the central value `a`. The **vacuum module** is
the module induced from the trivial character of the nonnegative currents `L[[t]]`,

`V = Ind_{L[[t]] ⊕ R K}^{ĝ} R = U / I₀`,

where `I₀ = U · ι(L[[t]])` is the left ideal generated by the currents of order at least `0`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.orderLeftIdeal`), so that `L[[t]]` kills the generator and `K` acts by
`a` (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.VacuumModule`). For `a = 1` and `Φ = -κ` this is the vacuum module
`V_κ(𝔤)` of the affine Kac--Moody algebra at level `κ`, the underlying space of the affine vertex
algebra. Its generator is the **vacuum vector** `|0⟩`, the class of `1`
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuum`).

This file gives the basic structure of `V`.

* `V` is cyclic on `|0⟩`, and the annihilator of `|0⟩` is exactly `I₀`
  (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.smul_vacuum_eq_zero_iff`).
* **Universal property.** For every `U`-module `M`, a `U`-linear map `V → M` is the same as a vector
  of `M` killed by the currents of nonnegative order
  (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumHomEquiv`); this is Frobenius reciprocity for the induced module.
* **Current fields.** `V` is smooth, so each `x : L` has a current field
  `J^x(z) = ∑ₙ xₙ z^{-n-1}` on `V` (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.currentField`), and these are
  mutually local. The nonnegative modes kill the vacuum
  (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.ncoeff_currentField_vacuum_eq_zero`): `J^x(z)|0⟩` is a power series in
  `z`, whose constant term is the coefficient `J^x[[-1]]|0⟩ = x₋₁|0⟩`. This is the creation
  property of the generating fields of the affine vertex algebra.
* **Coordinate changes.** Over a field, an algebra automorphism `σ` of `K⟦X⟧` lifts to an algebra
  automorphism `σ̂` of `U` which substitutes `σ X` in the currents and preserves `I₀`
  (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.coordinateEnvelopingAut`). It therefore descends to `V`, giving a group
  homomorphism from the automorphisms of `K⟦X⟧` to the linear automorphisms of `V`
  (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumCoordinateAction`). The action of `σ` fixes `|0⟩` and is
  `σ̂`-semilinear, `σ · (u v) = σ̂(u) (σ · v)`, and these two properties determine it
  (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.eq_vacuumCoordinateAction`). This works at every central value,
  including the critical level.
* **PBW identification.** Over a field, `y ↦ y |0⟩` is a linear isomorphism from the enveloping
  algebra `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])` of the negative currents
  (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.negativeLieSubalgebra`) onto `V`
  (`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumPBWEquiv`), intertwining left multiplication with the action on
  `V`. So `V` is a free `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])`-module of rank one on `|0⟩`, and every basis of
  `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])`, such as an ordered PBW basis `Module.Basis.pbwBasis`, is carried to a basis of
  `V`. This holds at every central value, including the critical level and `a = 0`.

No finiteness of `L` is used, and except for the coordinate action and the PBW identification the
base ring is an arbitrary commutative ring.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.VacuumModule`: the vacuum module `U / I₀`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuum`: the vacuum vector.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumLift`: the `U`-linear map `V → M` sending `|0⟩` to a vector killed
  by the nonnegative currents.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumHomEquiv`: the universal property of the vacuum module.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumCoordinateAction`: the action of the automorphisms of `K⟦X⟧` on
  the vacuum module.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumPBWEquiv`: the PBW identification `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹]) ≃ V`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.smul_vacuum_eq_zero_iff`: the annihilator of the vacuum is `I₀`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.span_vacuum_eq_top`: the vacuum generates the vacuum module.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumModule_hom_ext`: `U`-linear maps out of `V` agree once they agree
  on the vacuum.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.ncoeff_currentField_vacuum_eq_zero`: the nonnegative modes of the current
  fields kill the vacuum.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumCoordinateAction_smul`: the coordinate action is semilinear along
  the lift to `U`.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.eq_vacuumCoordinateAction`: it is the unique such map fixing the vacuum.
* `TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumPBWEquiv_mul`: the PBW identification intertwines left
  multiplication on `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])` with the action on the vacuum module.

## References

* E. Frenkel, D. Ben-Zvi, *Vertex Algebras and Algebraic Curves*, 2nd ed., §2.4, for the vacuum
  module of an affine Kac--Moody algebra, its current fields and the vacuum axiom.
* E. Frenkel, *Langlands Correspondence for Loop Groups*, §2.2, for the vacuum module `V_κ(𝔤)`
  as an induced module, and Chapter 3 for the action of the group `Aut O` of coordinate changes.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open scoped LaurentSeries VertexOperator
open PowerSeries LieAlgebra TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra
open LieAlgebra.ofTwoCocycle (centralElement envelopingι)

attribute [local instance 1100] HahnSeries.instAlgebra

namespace TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra

section Vacuum

variable {R L : Type*} [CommRing R] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra R L]
variable (Φ : LinearMap.BilinForm R L) (hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L) (hΦs : Φ.IsSymm) (a : R)

local notation "c" => twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs
local notation "UK" => CentralQuotient R (centralElement c) a

/-- The **vacuum module** `V = U / I₀` of the residue central extension of `Φ` at the central
value `a`: the module induced from the character of `L[[t]] ⊕ R K` which kills the nonnegative
currents and sends `K` to `a`. It is the quotient of the left regular module of
`U = U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)` by the left ideal `I₀` generated by the currents of order at least `0`. -/
abbrev VacuumModule : Type _ :=
  UK ⧸ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0

/-- The **vacuum vector** `|0⟩` of the vacuum module, the class of `1`. -/
def vacuum : VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a :=
  Submodule.Quotient.mk 1

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a}

/-- The class of `u` in the vacuum module is `u |0⟩`. -/
@[simp]
theorem mk_eq_smul_vacuum (u : UK) :
    (Submodule.Quotient.mk u : VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a) = u • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a := by
  rw [vacuum, ← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]

/-- **The annihilator of the vacuum is `I₀`:** `u |0⟩ = 0` exactly when `u` lies in the left ideal
generated by the currents of nonnegative order. -/
@[simp]
theorem smul_vacuum_eq_zero_iff {u : UK} :
    u • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a = 0 ↔ u ∈ orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0 := by
  rw [← mk_eq_smul_vacuum, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]

/-- The currents of nonnegative order kill the vacuum. -/
@[simp]
theorem envelopingι_smul_vacuum {u : currentAlgebra R L} (hu : u ∈ orderSubmodule R L 0) :
    envelopingι c a u • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a = 0 :=
  smul_vacuum_eq_zero_iff.2 (envelopingι_mem_orderLeftIdeal hu)

/-- Every vector of the vacuum module is `u |0⟩` for some `u`. -/
theorem exists_smul_vacuum_eq (v : VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a) :
    ∃ u : UK, u • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a = v := by
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ v
  exact ⟨u, (mk_eq_smul_vacuum u).symm⟩

/-- **The vacuum generates the vacuum module.** -/
theorem span_vacuum_eq_top : Submodule.span UK {vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a} = ⊤ :=
  (Submodule.span_singleton_eq_top_iff _ _).2 exists_smul_vacuum_eq

section Lift

variable {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M]
  [Module (CentralQuotient R (centralElement (twoCocycleOfBilinear R L Φ hΦ hΦs)) a) M]

/-- The `U`-linear map from the vacuum module sending `|0⟩` to a vector `m` killed by the currents
of nonnegative order. -/
def vacuumLift (m : M) (hm : ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L 0, envelopingι c a u • m = 0) :
    VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a →ₗ[UK] M :=
  (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0).liftQ (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton UK M m)
    (orderLeftIdeal_le_iff.2 fun u hu ↦ hm u hu)

/-- The lift sends `u |0⟩` to `u m`. -/
theorem vacuumLift_smul_vacuum (m : M)
    (hm : ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L 0, envelopingι c a u • m = 0) (u : UK) :
    vacuumLift m hm (u • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) = u • m := by
  rw [← mk_eq_smul_vacuum, vacuumLift, Submodule.liftQ_apply, LinearMap.toSpanSingleton_apply]

/-- The lift sends the vacuum to `m`. -/
@[simp]
theorem vacuumLift_vacuum (m : M)
    (hm : ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L 0, envelopingι c a u • m = 0) :
    vacuumLift m hm (vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) = m := by
  simpa using vacuumLift_smul_vacuum m hm 1

/-- `U`-linear maps out of the vacuum module are determined by their value on the vacuum. -/
@[ext]
theorem vacuumModule_hom_ext {f g : VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a →ₗ[UK] M}
    (h : f (vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) = g (vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a)) : f = g := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun v ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := exists_smul_vacuum_eq v
  rw [map_smul, map_smul, h]

/-- **The universal property of the vacuum module.** For a module `M` over `U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)`,
evaluation at the vacuum identifies the `U`-linear maps `V → M` with the vectors of `M` killed by
the currents of nonnegative order. -/
def vacuumHomEquiv : (VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a →ₗ[UK] M) ≃
    {m : M // ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L 0, envelopingι c a u • m = 0} where
  toFun f := ⟨f (vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a), fun u hu ↦ by
    rw [← map_smul, envelopingι_smul_vacuum hu, map_zero]⟩
  invFun m := vacuumLift m.1 m.2
  left_inv f := vacuumModule_hom_ext (vacuumLift_vacuum _ _)
  right_inv m := Subtype.ext (vacuumLift_vacuum _ _)

/-- The universal property evaluates at the vacuum. -/
@[simp]
theorem vacuumHomEquiv_apply_coe (f : VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a →ₗ[UK] M) :
    (vacuumHomEquiv f : M) = f (vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) :=
  (rfl)

/-- The inverse of the universal property is `vacuumLift`. -/
@[simp]
theorem vacuumHomEquiv_symm_apply
    (m : {m : M // ∀ u ∈ orderSubmodule R L 0, envelopingι c a u • m = 0}) :
    vacuumHomEquiv.symm m = vacuumLift m.1 m.2 :=
  (rfl)

end Lift

/-- **The vacuum axiom for current fields.** The nonnegative modes `J^x[[n]] = xₙ` of the current
field of `x` on the vacuum module kill the vacuum, so `J^x(z)|0⟩` is a power series in `z`. -/
theorem ncoeff_currentField_vacuum_eq_zero (x : L) {n : ℤ} (hn : 0 ≤ n) :
    ((currentField (envelopingAction (M := VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a) Φ hΦ hΦs a)
      ((isSmooth_envelopingAction_iff Φ hΦ hΦs a).2
        (smoothModules_quotient_orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0)) x)[[n]])
        (vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) = 0 := by
  rw [ncoeff_currentField, envelopingAction_apply]
  exact envelopingι_smul_vacuum (tmul_mem_orderSubmodule R L 0
    (HahnSeries.orderTop_single_le.trans' (by exact_mod_cast hn)) x)

end Vacuum

section Coordinate

variable {K L : Type*} [Field K] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]
variable (Φ : LinearMap.BilinForm K L) (hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L) (hΦs : Φ.IsSymm) (a : K)

local notation "c" => twoCocycleOfBilinear K L Φ hΦ hΦs
local notation "UK" => CentralQuotient K (centralElement c) a

/-- The lift of a coordinate change, as a semilinear map of the left regular module, preserves
`I₀`. -/
private theorem orderLeftIdeal_le_comap_coordinateEnvelopingAut (σ : K⟦X⟧ ≃ₐ[K] K⟦X⟧) :
    orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0 ≤ (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0).comap
      (coordinateEnvelopingAut Φ hΦ hΦs a σ : UK →+* UK).toSemilinearMap :=
  fun _ hu ↦ (coordinateEnvelopingAut_mem_orderLeftIdeal_iff σ).2 hu

/-- The map induced on the vacuum module by the lift of a coordinate change. It is semilinear along
the lift `σ̂` and `K`-linear. -/
private def vacuumCoordinateMap (σ : K⟦X⟧ ≃ₐ[K] K⟦X⟧) :
    VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a →ₗ[K] VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a where
  toFun := (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0).mapQ (orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a 0)
    (coordinateEnvelopingAut Φ hΦ hΦs a σ : UK →+* UK).toSemilinearMap
    (orderLeftIdeal_le_comap_coordinateEnvelopingAut Φ hΦ hΦs a σ)
  map_add' := map_add _
  map_smul' r v := by
    rw [← algebraMap_smul UK r v, LinearMap.map_smulₛₗ, RingHom.coe_coe, AlgEquiv.commutes,
      algebraMap_smul, RingHom.id_apply]

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a}

/-- The induced map sends `u |0⟩` to `σ̂(u) |0⟩`. -/
private theorem vacuumCoordinateMap_smul_vacuum (σ : K⟦X⟧ ≃ₐ[K] K⟦X⟧) (u : UK) :
    vacuumCoordinateMap Φ hΦ hΦs a σ (u • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) =
      coordinateEnvelopingAut Φ hΦ hΦs a σ u • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a := by
  rw [← mk_eq_smul_vacuum, ← mk_eq_smul_vacuum]
  exact Submodule.mapQ_apply (h := orderLeftIdeal_le_comap_coordinateEnvelopingAut Φ hΦ hΦs a σ)
    _ _ _ u

/-- The induced maps compose as the coordinate changes do. -/
private theorem vacuumCoordinateMap_mul_apply (σ τ : K⟦X⟧ ≃ₐ[K] K⟦X⟧)
    (v : VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a) :
    vacuumCoordinateMap Φ hΦ hΦs a (σ * τ) v =
      vacuumCoordinateMap Φ hΦ hΦs a σ (vacuumCoordinateMap Φ hΦ hΦs a τ v) := by
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := exists_smul_vacuum_eq v
  simp [vacuumCoordinateMap_smul_vacuum]

/-- The identity coordinate change induces the identity. -/
private theorem vacuumCoordinateMap_one_apply (v : VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a) :
    vacuumCoordinateMap Φ hΦ hΦs a 1 v = v := by
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := exists_smul_vacuum_eq v
  simp [vacuumCoordinateMap_smul_vacuum]

variable (Φ hΦ hΦs a)

/-- **Coordinate changes on the vacuum module.** An algebra automorphism `σ` of `K⟦X⟧` acts on the
vacuum module through its lift `σ̂` to `U(ĝ) / (ι K - a)`, by `u |0⟩ ↦ σ̂(u) |0⟩`; this is well
defined because `σ̂` preserves `I₀`. The action is a group homomorphism for the product
`σ * τ = σ ∘ τ`. -/
def vacuumCoordinateAction :
    (K⟦X⟧ ≃ₐ[K] K⟦X⟧) →* (VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a ≃ₗ[K] VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a) where
  toFun σ := LinearEquiv.ofLinearMap (vacuumCoordinateMap Φ hΦ hΦs a σ)
    (vacuumCoordinateMap Φ hΦ hΦs a σ⁻¹)
    (LinearMap.ext fun v ↦ by
      rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, ← vacuumCoordinateMap_mul_apply, mul_inv_cancel,
        vacuumCoordinateMap_one_apply, LinearMap.id_apply])
    (LinearMap.ext fun v ↦ by
      rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, ← vacuumCoordinateMap_mul_apply, inv_mul_cancel,
        vacuumCoordinateMap_one_apply, LinearMap.id_apply])
  map_one' := LinearEquiv.ext vacuumCoordinateMap_one_apply
  map_mul' σ τ := LinearEquiv.ext (vacuumCoordinateMap_mul_apply σ τ)

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a}

/-- The coordinate change `σ` sends `u |0⟩` to `σ̂(u) |0⟩`. -/
@[simp]
theorem vacuumCoordinateAction_smul_vacuum (σ : K⟦X⟧ ≃ₐ[K] K⟦X⟧) (u : UK) :
    vacuumCoordinateAction Φ hΦ hΦs a σ (u • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) =
      coordinateEnvelopingAut Φ hΦ hΦs a σ u • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a :=
  vacuumCoordinateMap_smul_vacuum σ u

/-- **Coordinate changes fix the vacuum.** -/
@[simp]
theorem vacuumCoordinateAction_vacuum (σ : K⟦X⟧ ≃ₐ[K] K⟦X⟧) :
    vacuumCoordinateAction Φ hΦ hΦs a σ (vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) = vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a := by
  simpa using vacuumCoordinateAction_smul_vacuum σ 1

/-- **The coordinate action is semilinear along the lift to `U`:** `σ (u v) = σ̂(u) (σ v)`. In
particular `σ (xₙ v)` is the substituted current `σ̂(xₙ)` applied to `σ v`. -/
theorem vacuumCoordinateAction_smul (σ : K⟦X⟧ ≃ₐ[K] K⟦X⟧) (u : UK)
    (v : VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a) :
    vacuumCoordinateAction Φ hΦ hΦs a σ (u • v) =
      coordinateEnvelopingAut Φ hΦ hΦs a σ u • vacuumCoordinateAction Φ hΦ hΦs a σ v := by
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := exists_smul_vacuum_eq v
  rw [smul_smul, vacuumCoordinateAction_smul_vacuum, vacuumCoordinateAction_smul_vacuum, map_mul,
    mul_smul]

/-- **Uniqueness of the coordinate action.** A map of the vacuum module which is semilinear along
the lift `σ̂` of `σ` and fixes the vacuum is the action of `σ`. -/
theorem eq_vacuumCoordinateAction (σ : K⟦X⟧ ≃ₐ[K] K⟦X⟧)
    {f : VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a → VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a}
    (hf : ∀ (u : UK) v, f (u • v) = coordinateEnvelopingAut Φ hΦ hΦs a σ u • f v)
    (hf₀ : f (vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) = vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) :
    f = vacuumCoordinateAction Φ hΦ hΦs a σ := by
  funext v
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := exists_smul_vacuum_eq v
  rw [hf, hf₀, vacuumCoordinateAction_smul_vacuum]

end Coordinate

section PBW

variable {K L : Type*} [Field K] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]
variable (Φ : LinearMap.BilinForm K L) (hΦ : Φ.lieInvariant L) (hΦs : Φ.IsSymm) (a : K)

local notation "c" => twoCocycleOfBilinear K L Φ hΦ hΦs
local notation "UK" => CentralQuotient K (centralElement c) a
local notation "Uneg" => UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K (negativeLieSubalgebra Φ hΦ hΦs)

/-- **The PBW identification of the vacuum module.** Over a field, `y ↦ y |0⟩` is a linear
isomorphism from the enveloping algebra `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])` of the negative currents onto the vacuum
module, for every form `Φ` and every central value `a`, including the critical level and `a = 0`.
It intertwines left multiplication on `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])` with the action on the vacuum module
(`TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra.vacuumPBWEquiv_mul`), so the vacuum module is a free module of rank one
over `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])` on the vacuum. -/
def vacuumPBWEquiv : Uneg ≃ₗ[K] VacuumModule Φ hΦ hΦs a :=
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    ((LinearMap.toSpanSingleton UK _ (vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a)).restrictScalars K ∘ₗ
      (negativeEnvelopingHom Φ hΦ hΦs a).toLinearMap)
    ⟨(injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).2 fun y hy ↦ by
      simpa using smul_vacuum_eq_zero_iff.1 hy,
    fun v ↦ by
      obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := exists_smul_vacuum_eq v
      obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := exists_sub_negativeEnvelopingHom_mem_orderLeftIdeal Φ hΦ hΦs a u
      refine ⟨y, ?_⟩
      rw [← smul_vacuum_eq_zero_iff, sub_smul, sub_eq_zero] at hy
      simp [hy]⟩

variable {Φ hΦ hΦs a}

/-- The PBW identification sends `y` to `y |0⟩`. -/
@[simp]
theorem vacuumPBWEquiv_apply (y : Uneg) :
    vacuumPBWEquiv Φ hΦ hΦs a y = negativeEnvelopingHom Φ hΦ hΦs a y • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a :=
  (rfl)

/-- The inverse of the PBW identification sends `y |0⟩` back to `y`. -/
@[simp]
theorem vacuumPBWEquiv_symm_smul_vacuum (y : Uneg) :
    (vacuumPBWEquiv Φ hΦ hΦs a).symm (negativeEnvelopingHom Φ hΦ hΦs a y • vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a) =
      y :=
  (LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq _).2 (vacuumPBWEquiv_apply y).symm

/-- The PBW identification sends `1` to the vacuum. -/
theorem vacuumPBWEquiv_one : vacuumPBWEquiv Φ hΦ hΦs a 1 = vacuum Φ hΦ hΦs a := by
  simp

/-- The PBW identification intertwines left multiplication on `U(t⁻¹ L[t⁻¹])` with the action on
the vacuum module. -/
theorem vacuumPBWEquiv_mul (y y' : Uneg) :
    vacuumPBWEquiv Φ hΦ hΦs a (y * y') =
      negativeEnvelopingHom Φ hΦ hΦs a y • vacuumPBWEquiv Φ hΦ hΦs a y' := by
  simp [mul_smul]

end PBW

end TauCeti.CurrentAlgebra
